UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventescapetothegrapes25167-20260412@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261018T135423Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260412
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:Escape to the Grapes
DESCRIPTION:Frederick’s Finest Double-Decker Winery Tour This one-of-a-kind Frederick winery tour carries you to two of the region’s most beautiful Maryland vineyards\, where glasses sparkle\, conversation flows\, and the word “bouquet” is pronounced with unnecessary confidence. Sip\, swirl\, and pretend you know what “oaky undertones” means as you gaze across rolling hills that seem purpose-built for day-drinking. Between tastings\, our Routemaster cruises through Frederick County with sweeping views\, witty commentary\, and occasional confusion about left-hand traffic. It’s part history lesson\, part holiday\, and entirely the wrong environment for anyone who dislikes laughter. Escape to the Grapes is the perfect mix of vineyard sightseeing\, Maryland wine tastings\, and double-decker absurdity. So grab your tickets\, summon your inner sommelier\, and come experience Frederick’s best winery bus tour\, where elegance meets hilarity and the countryside never looked so bubbly It’s going to be a corker of a day—cheers to that!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/escape-to-the-grapes/25167/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventboat26brewkayak26visittosmoketownbrewery20803-20260620@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261018T135423Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260620
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:Boat & Brew - Kayak & Visit to Smoketown Brewery
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a beautiful\, guided paddle on a 5.5-mile stretch of the Potomac River where Great Blue Herons and other wildlife are often spotted. Continue your journey and partake in a craft beer tasting at Smoketown Brewing Station after your kayaking trip. Enjoy a flight of tasty beer in an upbeat environment\, with seating available in the tasting room or the outside patio. Tour behind the glass wall and speak to the brewery team about Smoketown's hand-crafted beer. Trip includes a tasty flight and personal pizza. Add on to a great day with Smoketown's delicious food selections like their \\
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/boat-%26-brew-kayak-%26-visit-to-smoketown-brewery/20803/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfallfunfestivalatgaverfarm20763-20260904@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261018T135423Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Fall Fun Festival at Gaver Farm
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the vibrant colors and crisp air of autumn at the Fall Fun Festival at Gaver Farm! Running throughout September and October\, this family-friendly event offers over 65 exciting attractions\, making it the perfect destination for a day of fun\, laughter\, and unforgettable memories. Explore the Corn Maze. It’s a 7-acre corn maze\, perfect for all ages. This maze combines the thrill of exploration with the joy of discovery. Whether you’re working together as a family or racing against friends\, our corn maze promises a day of fun and excitement. Meet Our Friendly Barnyard Animals: Get up close and personal with our friendly barnyard animals\, including goats\, sheep\, cow\, alpacas\, pigs\, donkey\, pony\, bunnies\, peacocks\, turkeys\, ducks and chickens. Kids (and adults!) love the opportunity to feed and interact with our goats\, creating cherished memories and learning about farm life along the way. Fall Fun Fest Admission is $20.50 per person on September weekends\, $24.00 per person on October weekends\, and $14.50 per person on weekdays. Kids under 24 months are free. Tickets are available online and in person at the farm.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/fall-fun-festival-at-gaver-farm/20763/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfallfestivalatmagnoliameadowfarms17423-20260926@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261018T135423Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260926
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Fall Festival at Magnolia Meadow Farms
DESCRIPTION:Your Fall Starts Here! Home to Maryland’s Largest Corn Maze\, we’re more than just a pumpkin patch! Located in beautiful Northern Frederick County\, just 1 hour west of Baltimore and 1.5 hours north of D.C. Come spend a day on the farm with something for everyone to enjoy! Maryland’s Largest Corn Maze with over 5 miles of trails\, PLUS: Famous Apple Cannons Hayrides to the Pumpkin Patch Farm Animal Interactions Gem Mining Mini Ziplines Jumping Pillow Mountain Slides Pedal Karts PICK-YOUR-OWN: Sunflowers Cut flowers and wildflowers Pumpkins in all shapes\, sizes\, & colors! GATHER: Share stories around a Private Campfire! Live entertainment every Saturday & Sunday! EAT: Enjoy a farm fresh meal with local beef\, pork\, and poultry! Freshly Made Apple Cider Donuts Freshly Made Kettle Corn Beer & Wine (21+\, ID required) SHOP: Pick up locally made products! Farm Fresh Honey Goat Milk Soap Baked Goods Magnolia Meadow Farms t-shirts\, sweatshirts\, & hats HOURS: September 26 - November 1 Saturdays: 10:00am to 8:00pm Sundays: 10:00am to 6:00pm Check our website for special days & hours!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/fall-festival-at-magnolia-meadow-farms/17423/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventsummersfarmfallfestival12916-20260926@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261018T135423Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260926
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Summers Farm Fall Festival
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our annual Fall Festival at Summers Farm! For over 30 years\, Summers Farm has been the go-to destination for fall fun in Frederick County\, Maryland. With 45+ exciting activities\, there’s something for everyone to enjoy! Whether you're planning a day of family fun\, a corporate outing\, a school field trip\, an adventurous day date\, or just some good old-fashioned fun—Summers Farm is the place to be this fall! Here's what we have planned: Pumpkin Train Photo Ops Specialty Food & Drinks Famous Corn Maze Petting Zoo Wagon Rides Pedal Car Track Giant Slides Local Food Vendors 45+ Attractions & so much more! September 26 – November 1 September Sat – Sun: 10am – 7pm October 1 – 4 Thurs – Sun: 1pm – 7pm (Thurs)\, 1pm – 9pm (Fri)\, 10am – 9pm (Sat)\, 10am – 7pm (Sun) October 7 – 31 Wed – Thurs: 1pm – 7pm Fri: 1pm – 9pm Sat: 10am – 9pm Sun: 10am – 7pm November 1 (Sunday only) 10am – 7pm *October 12\, 16 & 26th – School Daze Craze: 11:30am – 9pm
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/summers-farm-fall-festival/12916/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventpumpkinpatchatmaynes24117-20261001@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261018T135423Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Pumpkin Patch At Mayne's
DESCRIPTION:Pumpkin Patch At Mayne's Celebrate Fall at Mayne's Tree Farm Pumpkin Patch in Frederick\, MD. Our pumpkin patch is open for the month of October on weekdays from 10a.m. - 6p.m. and on the weekends from 10a.m. - 5p.m. Pumpkins are available in small\, medium and large. Large groups by appointment during the week. Click Here for our full events schedule on facebook! Fall Activities Include: Hayrides To The Patch Corn Maze Apple Cider Scarecrow Making Straw Jumpin Antique Tractor Display For Your Fall Decoration Needs We Offer: Gourds ~ Mini Pumpkins ~ Indian Corn ~ Corn Stalks ~ Straw Bales
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/pumpkin-patch-at-maynes/24117/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventbackfromthedeadcemeterywalk8942-20261009@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261018T135423Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Back from the Dead Cemetery Walk
DESCRIPTION:On this unique and popular Cemetery Walk\, as a guide leads you through the dark by candlelight\, saints and other characters come to life and reflect upon the “Last Things”: death\, judgement\, heaven\, and hell. Through these encounters you’ll discover what it means to truly be alive\, both now and in the life to come. This faith-filled walk is ideal for youth groups and families with older children (14+). What to expect on the outdoor Cemetery Walk: This walking experience lasts for 1 hour and takes place primarily in the dark. All paths are wheelchair / stroller accessible. No seating is available throughout the experience. In the event of inclement weather\, all tickets will be refunded or rescheduled to another night\, pending availability.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/back-from-the-dead-cemetery-walk/8942/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventtrailofjackolanternswithtrickortreating9284-20261016@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261018T135423Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Trail of Jack-O-Lanterns with Trick or Treating
DESCRIPTION:Looking for something fun to do with the children this October that won’t scare them and is appropriate for any age? You found it! Join us 6pm to 10pm for our walking Trail of Jack-O-Lanterns. Admission is $16.00\, credit only ages 2 and older (babies are free) & includes our Trail\, fire pits\, and our Animal Barn (open 6pm to 9:00pm.) to see your furry friends. Admission will also include trick or treating for children from 7pm to 8pm. The Trail closes at 9pm. Bring your children (and your adults) in costume to add to the fun! Available for purchase will be night hayrides\, pumpkin flashlights\, Trick or Treat bags\, glow necklaces\, and more! Gates open 5:30pm. Last admission is 8:30pm. Check our website for NEW nightly specials! Dates: Oct 16\, 17\, 18\, 23\, 24\, 25\, 30 and 31\, 2026 (weather permitting) NOTE: The Trail is a separate event from our daytime petting farm and requires a separate\, new admission to enter.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/trail-of-jack-o-lanterns-with-trick-or-treating/9284/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
