BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventlostcemeteriesoffrederickcitywalkingtour26189-20261018@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261018T135423Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Lost Cemeteries of Frederick City Walking Tour
DESCRIPTION:Do you know you could be standing on ground that was once a graveyard? As cities change and grow\, its burial sites do as well. Join us as we investigate this hidden map of moving cemeteries. We will traipse through the courtyards and alleyways you may be familiar with to explore hidden burial grounds\, many of which have been disturbed. You will discover secrets that you have never suspected as you have moved about our fair city.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/lost-cemeteries-of-frederick-city-walking-tour/26189/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventmoonfestivalalice25830-20261018@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261018T135423Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:Moon Festival Alice
DESCRIPTION:MET's FUN COMPANY PRESENTS: Moon Festival Alice - A MET Original A curious child falls down a rabbit hole during a Mid-Autumn Festival celebration and enters a magical world inspired by Asian folklore\, festivals\, and modern Asian American life. Presented in partnership with The Asian American Center of Frederick. RUN TIME: Around an hour with no intermission.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/moon-festival-alice/25830/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventtheroadslesstraveled3atherusticroadsinfrederickcounty26218-20261018@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261018T135423Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:The Roads Less Traveled: The Rustic Roads in Frederick County
DESCRIPTION:Frederick County’s Road system is dominated by modern well-paved thoroughfares. However\, tucked away among the county's towns and farms\, including some in the Middletown Valley\, are rustic roads dating back to the mid-1700s. Susan Hanson will discuss the rich history of these historic pathways and efforts to preserve them. Susan Hanson was the founder of The Friends of Rural Roads and has been a leading advocate for the preservation of Frederick County’s rustic roads for over 25 years. She operated her own business\, Catoctin Pottery\, in the historic Lewis Mill for 40 years. At present\, she is the Vice Chair of Frederick County’s Rustic Roads Commission.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/the-roads-less-traveled%3a-the-rustic-roads-in-frederick-county/26218/
END:VEVENT
